                <pb facs="0891" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.1111Sh4/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi>, (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-08T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 9:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>6. A. L. Shelton, missionary doctor, Foreign Christian Missionary Society,
                    kidnaped by brigands January 3rd, traveling Batang to Yunnanfu, two days journey
                    from the latter place. Reported held for ransom. Wife and two daughters safe.
                    Further details <pb facs="0892" n="794" xml:id="pg794"/> lacking. Have requested
                    cooperation of French consul, Yunnanfu, and have telegraphed to local governor.
                    Will keep the Department fully informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
